    "video": {
      "name": "Keto Cloud Bread Roll Ups [Super Easy Low-Carb Lunch]",
      "description": "Growing up my mom used to make tortilla roll ups with cream cheese, taco seasoning, cheddar cheese, and black olives. Man, do I miss those. Of course, I had to create a new keto version of these tasty snacks!\n\nWhile the base of those rolled up tortillas were absolutely not keto, I knew I had to tackle this problem first. The base of this is made out of whipped eggs and cream cheese, which is baked for about 15 minutes. I then add the fixings inside and roll it up, mainly so the base doesn’t break, but it also gives me a nice warm snack to enjoy over the cold ones my mom used to make.\n\nRead the full recipe with full nutrition breakdown and step-by-step pictures over at:\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nIngredients:\n3 large egg, separated\n2 tablespoon cream cheese\n1 1/2 ounce cheddar cheese, sliced\n1 1/2 ounce deli-sliced salami\n\nNutrition Summary: This makes a total of 3 servings of Keto Cloud Bread Roll Ups. Each serving comes out to be 223 calories, 17.7g fat, 1.3g net carbs, and 13.7g protein.\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSee more keto recipes, knowledge and tips on the website to keep your weight loss going strong.\n\nEverything you need to know about the keto diet:\n\nGetting started? Everything you need is here:\n\nWe also make things easy with this 14 day diet plan:\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nFollow Ruled.Me for more tasty food:",
